  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "For any zero-indexed sequence SSS of length NNN, define a function G(S)G(S)G(S) as follows:\n\nG(S)=∏i=0N−1(Si+i)G(S) = \\prod_{i=0}^{N-1} (S_i + i)G(S)=i=0∏N−1​(Si​+i)If N=0N = 0N=0, then G(S)=1G(S) = 1G(S)=1, i.e. the empty sequence has a value of 111.\n\nFor an array BBB and a parameter KKK, we also define another function F(B,K)F(B, K)F(B,K) as follows:\n\nF(B,K)=∑G(S)F(B, K) = \\sum G(S)F(B,K)=∑G(S)where the summation is taken over all subsequences SSS of BBB such that ∣S∣=K|S| = K∣S∣=K.\n\nYou have an array BBB, which is initially empty.\n\nFor each iii from 111 to NNN, solve the following problem:\n\n\nYou are given two integers XiX_iXi​ and KiK_iKi​.\n\nFirst, insert XiX_iXi​ to the **front** of array BBB; so that we now have B=[Xi,Xi−1,…,X1]B = [X_i, X_{i-1}, \\ldots, X_1]B=[Xi​,Xi−1​,…,X1​].\n\nThen, compute\n∑j=0Ki(Ki+1−j)2⋅F(B,j)\\sum_{j = 0}^{K_i} (K_i + 1 - j)^2 \\cdot F(B, j)j=0∑Ki​​(Ki​+1−j)2⋅F(B,j)Since the answers can be very large, output them modulo 998 244 353998\\,244\\,353998244353.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nThe first line of input will contain a single integer TTT, denoting the number of test cases.\nEach test case consists of two lines of input.\n\nThe first line of each test case contains a single integer NNN.\nThe iii-th of the next NNN lines contains two integers XiX_iXi​ and KiK_iKi​, denoting the iii-th element to be inserted into AAA and the parameter for the iii-th query, respectively.\n\n\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, output NNN lines - the iii-th line must contain the answer corresponding to KiK_iKi​ after insertion of XiX_iXi​ to the **front** of BBB, modulo 998 244 353998\\,244\\,353998244353.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1031 \\leq T \\leq 10^31≤T≤103",
      "1≤N≤1051 \\leq N \\leq 10^51≤N≤105",
      "1≤Ki≤10001 \\leq K_i \\leq 10001≤Ki​≤1000",
      "1≤Xi≤1091 \\leq X_i \\leq 10^91≤Xi​≤109",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases dosen't exceed 10510^5105."
    ],
