        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111:\n\nAfter the first insertion, B=[1]B = [1]B=[1].\nIts subsequences are [],[1][], [1][],[1]; so we have F(B,0)=1,F(B,1)=1F(B, 0) = 1, F(B, 1) = 1F(B,0)=1,F(B,1)=1.\nThe answer is 4⋅F(B,0)+1⋅F(B,1)=54 \\cdot F(B, 0) + 1 \\cdot F(B, 1) = 54⋅F(B,0)+1⋅F(B,1)=5.\nAfter the second insertion, B=[2,1]B = [2, 1]B=[2,1].\nWe have F(B,0)=1,F(B,1)=3,F(B,2)=4F(B, 0) = 1, F(B, 1) = 3, F(B, 2) = 4F(B,0)=1,F(B,1)=3,F(B,2)=4.\nThe answer is 9⋅F(B,0)+4⋅F(B,1)+1⋅F(B,0)=259 \\cdot F(B, 0) + 4 \\cdot F(B, 1) + 1 \\cdot F(B, 0) = 259⋅F(B,0)+4⋅F(B,1)+1⋅F(B,0)=25."
